MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo and bulb kit felt useful because it adds lighting control to the Alexa setup I already use; the camera also offers a home-monitoring function that connects with my earlier door alarm purchase.",
    "The compact desktop speakers fit my repeated interest in practical computer peripherals. The memory card and HDMI cable also fit devices I use, although I would need a specific capacity or cable-length need before buying them."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Fire TV Stick 4K repeats a need already covered by my recent 4K Max bundle, while the tablet adds a device I have not shown an immediate need for.",
    "Mac-compatible keyboard purchases do not establish that I use an iPhone or need AirPods. Likewise, buying external computer accessories does not mean I am building a desktop that needs a CPU cooler."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Alexa purchases seem to have been taken as interest in any Alexa device, but adding useful home functions appeals more than buying another streamer or moving Alexa into my car without a specific need.",
    "My computer-accessory history seems to have been stretched into interest in electronics generally, even when an item requires hardware or a project I have not indicated."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases matter for what I already have: the Fire TV bundle covers streaming, and the Echo Show stand suggests interest in making an existing device more useful.",
    "Compatibility and an immediate practical purpose matter to me. A storage upgrade, longer cable, or car accessory can fit my interests without being something I need to buy now."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in practical peripherals and Alexa devices, but sometimes confuse related products with useful additions to what I already own."
}
